# XCU ipcs
# Copyright (c) 2026 Nicholas Martin. All rights reserved.
#
# The whole utility is XSI-shaded. Whether any message queue, shared memory
# segment or semaphore set exists is not under the control of a script (no
# POSIX utility creates one), so the tests judge the introductory line, the
# selection of reports by -q, -m and -s, and the status. Column contents
# are not checked.

assertion  XCU.ipcs.001
anchor     utilities/ipcs.html#STDOUT
class      conditional
when       XSI
says       The first output line is "IPC status from" a source, "as of" and a
           date in the form of the POSIX-locale date output (weekday, month,
           day, time, zone, year), and ipcs exits with status zero.
test       t/001-intro-line.sh

assertion  XCU.ipcs.002
anchor     utilities/ipcs.html#OPTIONS
anchor     utilities/ipcs.html#STDOUT
class      conditional
when       XSI
says       With -q only the message queue report is written: after the first
           line the output mentions Message Queue and neither Shared Memory
           nor Semaphore.
test       t/002-queues-only.sh

assertion  XCU.ipcs.003
anchor     utilities/ipcs.html#OPTIONS
anchor     utilities/ipcs.html#STDOUT
class      conditional
when       XSI
says       With -m only the shared memory report is written: after the first
           line the output mentions Shared Memory and neither Message Queue
           nor Semaphore.
test       t/003-shared-memory-only.sh

assertion  XCU.ipcs.004
anchor     utilities/ipcs.html#OPTIONS
anchor     utilities/ipcs.html#STDOUT
class      conditional
when       XSI
says       With -s only the semaphore report is written: after the first line
           the output mentions Semaphore and neither Message Queue nor Shared
           Memory.
test       t/004-semaphores-only.sh

assertion  XCU.ipcs.005
anchor     utilities/ipcs.html#DESCRIPTION
anchor     utilities/ipcs.html#STDOUT
class      conditional
when       XSI
says       With none of -q, -m and -s all three reports are written, and the
           print options -a, -b, -c, -o, -p and -t, alone or with the
           selecting options, do not change which reports appear.
test       t/005-all-reports.sh

assertion  XCU.ipcs.006
anchor     utilities/ipcs.html#STDOUT
class      untestable
when       XSI
says       Each present facility is shown with the columns T, ID, KEY, MODE,
           OWNER, GROUP and, depending on the options, the creator, byte
           count, process ID and time columns, in the stated formats.
reason     No POSIX utility can create a message queue, shared memory segment
           or semaphore set for the report to describe, and a script cannot
           rely on what other processes created.
